[
  {
    "sha": "43931b2ff0acd1e06f451147f2841d21ed3d822c",
    "node_id": "C_kwDOVoU8JdoAKDQzOTMxYjJmZjBhY2QxZTA2ZjQ1MTE0N2YyODQxZDIxZWQzZDgyMmM",
    "commit": {
      "author": {
        "name": "Mike Kinney",
        "email": "mike.kinney@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-11-25T02:16:56Z"
      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "Mike Kinney",
        "email": "mike.kinney@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-11-25T02:16:56Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(wire): Wire Contour takes an exit pick\n\nThe wire took a start pick only. An exit pick was refused at the command\ndoor (\"this kind takes a start point only\").\n\n- `PickCapability::Threading` takes a start and an exit.\n- An open run ends at the end nearest the exit pick: the same line on the\n  same side, walked the other way when the pick names the first end.\n- A closed profile is cut all the way round as before, then the wire rides\n  its own kerf on to the path's point nearest the pick and leaves by a\n  straight lead-out to the pick.\n- Refused by name, never moved: a pick that names no end of an open run,\n  a pick on the wire path, nearer than the kerf offset, or on the product\n  side; an exit beside tabs, skims, a taper, a burnout or a 4-axis cut; an\n  exit on a DXF chain that is cut on its arcs.\n\nThe exit is a new module, `motion::wire_edm::exit`, over the existing\ngenerator. A cut without an exit pick does not enter it, so every shipped\nwire golden is byte-identical.\n\nFixes #3332\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
